    "page_content": "1. Purpose\nThis policy defines the methodology used to measure the value of Order Intake for multi-element arrangements. This\nversion supersedes v1.0 and introduces a weighted allocation methodology following Q1 2025 internal audit\nrecommendations.\n2. Scope\nApplies to all multi-element customer arrangements combining:\n- Hardware/Software (HW/SW) deliverables, AND\n- Services deliverables\n3. Definitions\nStandalone Selling Price (SSP): The price at which the Company would sell a deliverable separately under similar\ncircumstances.\nWeighted Factor: An adjustment factor applied per deliverable category to reflect margin and risk differences,\ndetermined annually by the Pricing Committee.\n4. Roles and Responsibilities",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "C:\\Users\\USER\\Desktop\\RAG\\output_pdfs\\POL-ORD-002_v2.0_Order-Intake-Value-SSP-Allocation.pdf",
