  {
    "page_content": "5. SSP Allocation Methodology\n5.1 Calculation Basis\nAllocation is performed using the Relative SSP method, under which a Weighted Factor is applied per deliverable\ncategory. This replaces the unweighted Standalone List Price method used in v1.0.\n5.2 Weighted Factor Determination\nThe Weighted Factor is determined annually by the Pricing Committee based on:\n- Historical margin performance by deliverable category\n- Delivery risk profile\n- Market comparables\n5.3 Allocation Formula\nStep 1 — Relative SSP: Relative SSP = SSP × Weighted Factor\nStep 2 — SSP Allocation: SSP Allocation = (Relative SSP ÷ Total Relative SSP) × Total Contract Value\nStep 3 — Variance Check: SSP % from Contract Value = (SSP Allocation - Proportional Contract Value) ÷\nProportional Contract Value × 100",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "C:\\Users\\USER\\Desktop\\RAG\\output_pdfs\\POL-ORD-002_v2.0_Order-Intake-Value-SSP-Allocation.pdf",
